«
@@ ============================================================
@@ SunGP — geographical position of the Sun: Greenwich hour angle, declination
@@ and semidiameter, from the approximate formulas of the US Naval Observatory.
@@ 
@@ Input : date time — date as YYYYMMDD, UT time as HH.MMSS.
@@ Output: GHA Dec SD.
@@ The USNO states about 1′ within two centuries of 2000, about one nautical
@@ mile of position.
@@ Angle mode and angle units setting are restored before returning.
@@ ============================================================

  → dat tme
  «
    @ Dates as decimals: on a DM32, integer dates are rejected (issue #1873)
    dat DUP TypeName "unit" == « UVAL » « » IFTE EVAL →Num 20000101. DDays
    DUP TypeName "unit" == « UVAL » « » IFTE EVAL
    tme HMS→ 24 / + 0.5 - →Num
    'AngleMode' RCL 'SetAngleUnits' RCL
    RAD NoAngleUnits
    Ⓒπ →Num 180 /
    → ddd amode aunits rdn
    «
      '(357.529+0.98560028*ddd)*rdn' EVAL '280.459+0.98564736*ddd' EVAL
      '(23.439-0.00000036*ddd)*rdn' EVAL
      → gan qml obl
      «
        '(qml+1.915*SIN(gan)+0.020*SIN(2*gan))*rdn' EVAL
        '1.00014-0.01671*COS(gan)-0.00014*COS(2*gan)' EVAL
        → lng dst
        «
          '(15*(18.697374558+24.06570982441908*ddd))-((COS(obl)*SIN(lng))∠(COS(lng)))/rdn' EVAL
          360 MOD 1_° *
          'ASIN(SIN(obl)*SIN(lng))/rdn' EVAL 1_° *
          '0.2666/dst' EVAL 1_° * 1_arcmin CONVERT
        »
      »
      amode EVAL IF aunits THEN SetAngleUnits ELSE NoAngleUnits END
    »
  »
»
